Below is a description of what’s happening and a minimal patch to fix the broken previews for URLs that contain commas, colons or other “unsafe” characters in their path. 

### What’s going wrong  
When Quarto builds the grid preview, it generates a URL for each preview image by calling `joinUrl(baseUrl, path)`. In the presence of commas or colons in the path (for example  
```
/5:4/w_1028,c_limit/koji-steak-1.jpg
```
), the browser ends up requesting an un-encoded URL which doesn’t actually map to anything on disk (or a CDN), so the `<img>` tag in the grid is broken.

### The fix  
We need to percent-encode each path segment before we re-stitch them back together. Edit `src/core/url.ts` so that `joinUrl` does exactly that:

